    "recommended_additional_secrets_via_ci_width_extrapolation": 22,
    "plain_language": "The two MDE curves disagree sharply at k=34: the calibrated-synthetic curve claims 100% detection power there, but the REAL observed L2+L5 effect (same 34 secrets) only detects 27% of the time -- the synthetic injection's uniform per-secret shift is a much cleaner signal than real per-secret heterogeneity, so the synthetic curve's 'k=20 is already enough' claim is treated here as an OPTIMISTIC LOWER BOUND, not an actionable target. The REAL curve itself never exceeds 32% detection across all tested k<=34 (no clear rising trend within the tested range, given real per-secret noise + limited sims), so it cannot pin down a 'crosses 80%' k either. The most defensible number here comes from a THIRD, independent cross-check: extrapolating the Step 3 1/sqrt(n) CI-width fit to find the n at which a ~0.06 point estimate's own CI width would plausibly clear zero (assuming the point estimate holds and the CI stays roughly symmetric) gives n~56 -- i.e. roughly 22 MORE secrets beyond the current 34, an EXTRAPOLATION-derived estimate distinct from either measured MDE curve above.",
